{#
    The head, once, for both layouts.

    `soul-boot.js` is not a module and is loaded first: it writes `data-theme`
    before the first paint, from the stored choice or the reader's own
    setting. Without it the switch has nothing to show and the choice is lost
    on the next page.
#}
<meta charset="utf-8" />
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
{#- The project's name once. On a landing page the two are the same, and
    "Soul Design System — Soul Design System" is a tab nobody wrote. -#}
<title>{{ title }}
    {%- if env.projectNode.title and title != env.projectNode.title %} — {{ env.projectNode.title }}{% endif -%}</title>
{#- The mark in the tab. One `<link>` per file the project configured, and the
    browser picks by the size it needs — which is how a mark drawn at three
    optical sizes reaches the slot it was drawn for. Written with `asset()`
    like the signet is, so the path is resolved from the page being rendered
    and a page below the root reaches the same file. -#}
{%- for icon in soul.favicons %}
<link rel="icon" href="{{ asset('/' ~ icon.href) }}"
      {%- if icon.type %} type="{{ icon.type }}"{% endif %}
      {%- if icon.sizes %} sizes="{{ icon.sizes }}"{% endif %} />
{%- endfor %}
<script src="{{ root }}styles/soul-boot.js"></script>
{#- The variable faces a page opens in. The preload starts them before the
    stylesheet is parsed; `font-display: optional` keeps a late response from
    replacing the fallback after paint. Each file covers every used weight. -#}
<link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin
      href="{{ root }}styles/fonts/source-sans-3-latin-wght-normal.woff2" />
<link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin
      href="{{ root }}styles/fonts/source-code-pro-latin-wght-normal.woff2" />
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ root }}styles/soul.css" />
<script type="module" src="{{ root }}styles/soul.js" defer></script>
